{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>The sons of Leah: the firstborn of Jacob, etc.</b> The reason it was necessary to inform us that he was the firstborn of Jacob, is to say that one should not think anything improper of him, since it is written nearby: ״וַיִּשְׁכַּב אֶת בִּלְהָה״ (Genesis 35:22) — for he did not actually lie with her. The proof is that Scripture went back and counted him together with the rest of his brothers, as it is written: ״וַיִּהְיוּ בְנֵי יַעֲקֹב שְׁנֵים עָשָׂר״ (Genesis 35:22). Therefore it specified and said <b>the firstborn of Jacob</b>, for he is the firstborn of Jacob, and by virtue of being the first drop of Jacob, this quality will firmly establish in him the banishment of repulsiveness and one will not suspect him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:11.221852314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}